---
/**
 * Multicellularity — first biology-lens concept at Collective scale.
 * Higher-order living system formed when many Cells stay coupled under shared organization.
 * Nested Boundaries: members keep membranes; the whole (e.g. Space Identity) has its own Boundary.
 * Order: Coupling → Multicellularity → Specialization → Regulation.
 * Keep inline tags on one line with outer spaces (Astro whitespace).
 * No em-dashes in public copy.
 */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const osCreationJurisdiction =
	'https://github.com/identity-engineering/os/blob/main/docs/identity-creation-jurisdiction.md';
---

<Layout title="Multicellularity | Identity Engineering">
	<main class="min-h-screen">
		<section class="min-h-[50vh] flex flex-col justify-center pt-28 pb-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40 mb-6">
					Biology lens · Collective Identity
				</div>
				<h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold tracking-tighter leading-[0.95] mb-6 text-white">
					Multicellularity
				</h1>
				<p class="text-xl text-white/50 font-light leading-relaxed mb-6">
					A higher-order living system: many Cells remain distinct and coupled,
					yet the whole persists as one organized form beyond any single pairwise link.
				</p>
				<div class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-500/20 bg-amber-500/[0.04] p-4">
					<p class="text-sm text-white/65 leading-relaxed">
						<strong class="text-white/80">Status:</strong> Working concept under the biology lens.
						Primary science reading: multicellular organism / tissue-scale organization.
						Analogy, not isomorphism. Follows Interactive
						<a href="/framework/coupling" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Coupling</a>;
						precedes Specialization and Regulation.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Definition</div>
				<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">The whole that outlasts the pair.</h2>
				<p>
					In biology, multicellularity is not merely many cells in contact.
					It is organization: cells remain individual units with membranes, yet participate in a
					<strong class="text-white/85">higher-order living form</strong> with shared architecture, division of labor, and collective persistence.
				</p>
				<p>
					In Identity Engineering, <strong class="text-white/85">Multicellularity</strong> names that scale jump under the biology lens.
					<a href="/framework/coupling" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Coupling</a>
					is still Interactive: sustained links between units that stay pairwise or local.
					Multicellularity begins when couplings densify into a
					<strong class="text-white/85">Collective Identity</strong> — a whole that can be recognized as one living system
					while its member Cells keep their own Boundaries.
				</p>
				<p>
					Under the physics lens this is close to
					<a href="/framework/emergent" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Emergence</a>:
					a higher-order object with its own persistence. Multicellularity is the living-form reading of that scale.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Nested membranes</div>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">Outer Boundary, member Boundaries</h2>
				<p>
					<a href="/framework/boundary" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Boundary</a>
					remains a Single-scale concept: every Identity has a membrane.
					Multicellularity does not invent a second Boundary primitive. It describes
					<strong class="text-white/85">nesting</strong>:
				</p>
				<ul class="space-y-4 text-lg">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Member Boundaries</strong> stay intact. Cells do not dissolve into one interior (that would be fusion, not multicellular organization).
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Outer Boundary of the whole</strong> is the Boundary of the collective Identity once
						<a href="/framework/emergent" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Emergence</a>
						gives that whole its own trajectory.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						In <a href="/os" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">IE OS</a>, a Space as collective host is exactly this pattern:
						member Identities keep Surfaces; the Space Identity carries membrane policy for the host.
						<strong class="text-white/85">Known is not addressable:</strong> a member may be registered or discoverable in a parent Space without granting others the right to call its Surface. Nested policy and creation-time jurisdiction grants decide the difference.
					</li>
				</ul>
				<p class="text-base text-white/50">
					Biology reading: tissue and organism organization (integument of the whole, membranes of the cells). Application of Boundary at Collective scale, not a rename of Boundary.
					OS contract:
					<a
						href={osCreationJurisdiction}
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener noreferrer"
						class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50"
					>identity-creation-jurisdiction.md</a>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">What Multicellularity is</div>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Collective living form:</strong> a higher-order Identity composed of coupled Cells.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Preserved members:</strong> constituent Cells remain bounded units; the whole does not require their dissolution.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Scale above Coupling:</strong> not only links, but an organized system that can persist as one.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Seat of later specialization and regulation:</strong> division of labor and multi-speed control belong to this scale next.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">What Multicellularity is not</div>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not a pile of Couplings.</strong>
						Many pairwise links without a higher-order form are still Interactive density, not Collective Identity.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not fusion into one Cell.</strong>
						If member Boundaries dissolve into a single interior, that is merger, not multicellular organization.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not a second Boundary concept.</strong>
						Outer membrane of the whole is Boundary of the collective Identity, not a Collective-only primitive.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not Specialization yet.</strong>
						Division of labor among member roles is the next concept. Multicellularity is the existence of the higher-order form.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not Regulation yet.</strong>
						Homeostatic and multi-speed control of the whole follows after roles exist.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not a claim that every group is an organism.</strong>
						Crowds and loose networks are not automatically multicellular Identity. Persistence and organization of the whole are required.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Order in the biology lens</div>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">Into Collective</h2>
				<ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-3 text-lg">
					<li>Interactive complete: Signal → Recognition → Coupling</li>
					<li><strong class="text-white/85">Multicellularity</strong> — higher-order living form from organized cells</li>
					<li>Specialization (next) — division of labor among member roles</li>
					<li>Regulation (after) — multi-speed control of the whole</li>
				</ol>
				<p>
					Multicellularity answers: <em class="text-white/75">when does a set of coupled Cells become one collective living system?</em>
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Engineering</div>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">What we work on</h2>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Name the whole without erasing members:</strong> collective Identity and member Cell both real.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Require organization, not only proximity:</strong> density of contact is not enough.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Hold the scale boundary:</strong> do not call every network an organism; do not reduce every organism to a bag of pairs.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Nest membranes explicitly:</strong> outer policy of the whole vs admission policy of each member.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Keep discovery and addressability distinct:</strong> nested Spaces may know members without making them publicly callable.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Prepare specialization:</strong> once the whole exists, roles can differentiate without abandoning multicellular form.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/55 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="rounded-2xl border border-cyan-400/20 bg-cyan-400/[0.04] p-6 text-base">
					<div class="mb-2 text-sm uppercase tracking-[3px] text-cyan-300/80">Science reading</div>
					<p>
						Primary discipline: <strong class="text-white/80">multicellular biology / organismal organization</strong>.
						Specialization and Regulation complete the Collective scale next.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 pt-4">
					<a href="/framework/coupling" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Coupling</a>
					<a href="/framework/boundary" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Boundary</a>
					<a href="/framework/emergent" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Emergence</a>
					<a href="/os" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">OS</a>
					<a href="/framework" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full bg-white text-black font-medium hover:bg-white/90 transition">Framework</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
</Layout>
